WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:06.803
The brain and spinal cord begin as a flat sheet of cells.

2
00:00:07.623 --> 00:00:10.443
By about the fourth week, how do they become a sealed tube?

3
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:15.447
This sheet is the neural plate, along the midline of the embryo's back.

4
00:00:16.327 --> 00:00:19.027
On either side, surface ectoderm will form the skin.

5
00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.410
Step one, shaping.

6
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:26.810
The cells grow taller, and the plate narrows from side to side and lengthens from

7
00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:27.810
head to tail.

8
00:00:28.483 --> 00:00:29.803
Hold on to this step.

9
00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:34.223
If the plate's middle stays wide, the folds may have too far to go.

10
00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:36.447
Step two, bending.

11
00:00:37.327 --> 00:00:41.267
The plate creases at hinge points, and its edges rise as the neural folds.

12
00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:46.657
Step three. The folds move toward the midline, meet, and fuse.

13
00:00:47.717 --> 00:00:52.317
Step four. The tube separates from the skin, which seals over it.

14
00:00:53.217 --> 00:00:54.397
Now look from above.

15
00:00:54.397 --> 00:00:59.497
In the mouse, closure begins at several sites and spreads from each like a zipper.

16
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.480
The first site is called Closure 1.

17
00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:06.600
It sits at the boundary between the hindbrain and the spinal cord.

18
00:01:10.033 --> 00:01:13.773
A stretch that does not close stays open for the rest of pregnancy.

19
00:01:14.553 --> 00:01:16.333
Where it stays open names the defect.

20
00:01:17.383 --> 00:01:20.583
If the head end fails, the result is anencephaly.

21
00:01:21.443 --> 00:01:23.443
The exposed brain tissue degenerates.

22
00:01:24.333 --> 00:01:28.313
If the lower end fails, the cord itself lies in an open lesion.

23
00:01:29.173 --> 00:01:32.653
This is myelomeningocele, the open form of spina bifida.

24
00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:38.623
In the mouse, if Closure 1 never happens, the tube stays open from the midbrain down

25
00:01:38.623 --> 00:01:41.563
the spine. This is craniorachischisis.

26
00:01:42.483 --> 00:01:43.843
So why would a tube fail?

27
00:01:44.763 --> 00:01:48.463
One reason: the folds can close only a gap their bending can cover.

28
00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:51.907
And the midline between them sets that gap.

29
00:01:52.867 --> 00:01:54.947
Narrowing it comes early and overlaps folding.

30
00:01:55.927 --> 00:01:58.807
Failures of bending, fusion or sealing are other routes.

31
00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.120
Takeaway: narrowing starts first and keeps going as the folds rise.

32
00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.700
Where closure fails names the defect.
